# Generated by gen_screen_sessions.py (rmgate, seed 2, 30 inputs): a seeded walk over the rmgate screen's keys and mouse; a state every 8 inputs
# wait:70 after a hold whose item shows a message (a difficulty, Music, Show Changes): the C# host's steps would otherwise come during the
# message's 60-tick wait (MessageBox.Show, root 0410:0302), where the original's tester gives none (local/batch/rcopus)
# key:f1..f3 after the Party hold on row 1 (Change Marching Order): they pick the members in R022+0x051C's box, which takes only F1..F5
# and left releases (without them both games stay in the box and state:end is taken inside the battle)
# the two Orders row 0 holds (Resume, rdown:115,4 move:119,16 and rdown:103,4 move:116,16) are left out: after the bar's Resume the
# original's next battle pass waits for the timer, so its tester gives the next key (bwait's idle rule) before any pass, while the C# host
# runs the key's frames as passes; the item itself (R016+0x1436) leaves the same pause state in both (local/batch/rcopus)
